    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d54">

                <pb facs="0114" n="64" sameAs="frus:frus1894/pg64"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Gresham to Senhor Mendonça</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1894-05-31"><hi rendition="#italic">May 31,
                        1894</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: At your interview with me yesterday you
                    communicated copy of a telegraphic instruction you had received from the
                    minister for foreign affairs, directing you to ask if the Government of the
                    United States would authorize its minister at Lisbon to protect Brazilian
                    citizens during the suspension of diplomatic relations with Portugal.</p>
                <p>Having taken the President’s directions in this regard, I have the pleasure to
                    inform you that the minister, of the United States at Lisbon will be instructed,
                    by cable, to use his friendly offices, with the acquiescence of the Portuguese
                    Government, for the protection of Brazilian citizens in Portugal or the
                    Portuguese dependencies during the present suspension of diplomatic relations
                    between those countries.</p>
                <p>Promising myself the further pleasure of communicating to you such reply as I may
                    receive from Mr. Caruth,</p>
                <p>I avail myself, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">W. Q. Gresham.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
